    "b-40k-target-2": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Every computed knowledge attachment hangs from a target. The graph is a rebuildable read model over the current target, project configuration, and knowledge ledger; it is not a write surface for agents."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40k-target-3": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Epoch lifecycle"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40k-target-4": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A completed live epoch runs full knowledge maintenance by default: graph tables reset and the current code base, configured indexes, and ledger learnings are ingested again. Dry runs, explicit skip modes, and no-rebuild operation can suppress that default."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40k-target-5": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-5",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Attachment",
          "Input",
          "As-built output"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Code graph",
            "Current target report and object-diff state, with stored indexes as fallback",
            "Files, units, functions, match state, editability, facts, edges, and search chunks"
          ],
          [
            "Call graph",
            "Symbolized branch-link and data-reference sites extracted from generated assembly",
            "CALLS and REFERENCES_DATA edges plus per-function profiles; only uniquely resolved current functions become edges"
          ],
          [
            "Siblings",
            "Bootstrapped Melee family rules plus the current function report",
            "SIBLING_OF edges and sibling profiles across fighter families that share a function stem"
          ],
          [
            "Ghidra xrefs",
            "Analyzed binary project",
            "Independent xref lookup used to check assembly-derived claims; it is not automatically joined into call-graph ingestion"
          ],
          [
            "Learnings",
            "Latest ledger record per learning ID",
            "Learning entities and search chunks; present anchors also receive HAS_LEARNING edges and learning_profile facts"
          ]
        ],
        "title": "Computed target attachments"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40k-target-6": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Present-anchored learning projection"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40k-target-7": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The learning builder skips refuted records and resolves symbol and file subjects against the current checkout. Existing anchors connect to learning entities through HAS_LEARNING and receive learning_profile facts. Area and general learnings remain searchable without a code anchor."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40k-target-8": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-8",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "title": "Missing anchors become stale",
        "tone": "decision"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A learning is preserved when its symbol or file disappears, but its projected status becomes stale. Missing symbol anchors cannot emit HAS_LEARNING or learning_profile; missing file subjects retain their file-shaped anchor ID and stale status. Nothing silently reattaches to a guessed replacement."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40k-target-9": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Rebuild guarantees"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40k-target-10": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-10",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Inputs remain authoritative; every graph row can be recreated from target artifacts, project rules, or ledger evidence."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40k-target-11": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-11",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Call and data-reference edges require unique resolution to a current function; unresolved observations stay in profiles rather than becoming misleading edges."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40k-target-12": {
      "id": "b-40k-target-12",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Sibling rules are Melee-owned configuration interpreted by a generic builder; bootstrapping the rules is a separate manual operation."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
